# Copy this file to .env (gitignored) and fill in real values to test real
# Entra ID (Azure AD) sign-in locally via `scripts/run-local.sh`.
#
# App registration requirements (see docs/DOTNET10_MIGRATION_PLAN.md section 4
# and the Decisions log for the reasoning - no client secret is needed since
# this app only authenticates users, it doesn't call any downstream API):
#   - Platform: Web
#   - Supported account types: Single tenant
#   - API permissions: default (openid, profile) - nothing extra needed
#   - Redirect URIs (add both so either launch profile works):
#       http://localhost:5234/signin-oidc
#       https://localhost:7234/signin-oidc
#   - Front-channel logout URLs:
#       http://localhost:5234/Account/SignOutCallback
#       https://localhost:7234/Account/SignOutCallback
#
# For the https launch profile (`scripts/run-local.sh --https`), you also
# need to have run `dotnet dev-certs https --trust` once on this machine.

AZURE_AD_TENANT_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
AZURE_AD_CLIENT_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
